---
// sip-engine.astro — SIP & Wealth Goal Accumulation Planner (Chassis Architecture)
// Single-entry point with 4-card input deck, transparent assumptions strip, mathematical verdict host, and multi-tab visual diagnostics.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SipInputForm from '../components/Calculators/SipInputForm.astro';
import SipAnswer from '../components/Calculators/SipAnswer.astro';
import SipWorking from '../components/Calculators/SipWorking.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SIP Accumulation Planner — Systematic Wealth Engine"
  description="Stress-test your systematic investment plan against 10,000 empirical market futures from the Nifty 50 record. Model real purchasing power, inflation step-up, LTCG tax, and Black-Scholes downside protection."
>
  <main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-4 pb-16 sm:pb-24 space-y-8">
    
    <!-- Editorial Page Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-navy-200/80 dark:border-navy-800/80 pb-6 space-y-2">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-gold-50 dark:bg-gold-950/40 text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-300 text-xs font-semibold">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gold-500"></span>
        <span>Systematic Wealth Accumulation Engine</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
        SIP & Wealth Goal Accumulation Planner
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Stress-test your systematic monthly savings against 10,000 empirical market paths from the 25-year Nifty 50 historical record. Model real purchasing power, annual career step-ups, LTCG taxation, and downside put floor protection.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <!-- Section 1: Interactive 4-Card Inputs Deck & Transparent Assumptions -->
      <section aria-label="SIP Accumulation plan inputs">
        <SipInputForm />
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Narrative Verdict & 1-Tap Levers (Central Compute Host) -->
      <section aria-label="Plan verdict and goal-seeking remedies">
        <SipAnswer />
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Visual Working & Multi-Tab Diagnostics -->
      <section aria-label="Visual working and simulation projections" class="w-full overflow-x-hidden">
        <SipWorking />
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Deep Dive Editorial Literature & Financial Mechanics -->
    <section class="space-y-12 pt-8 border-t border-navy-200/80 dark:border-navy-800/80">
      
      <!-- Section Header -->
      <div class="space-y-2 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 pb-5">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-gold-50 dark:bg-gold-950/40 text-gold-800 dark:text-gold-300 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
          Core Wealth Mechanics
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
          How Long-Term Wealth Accumulation Actually Works
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 max-w-4xl leading-relaxed">
          Wealth creation isn't magic—it follows predictable mathematical and economic rules. Below, we open the "black box" behind every formula used in this engine so you can see exactly how the gears turn, why traditional calculators mislead you, and how to protect your family's future purchasing power.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article 1: Real Purchasing Power vs Inflation Drag -->
      <article class="scroll-mt-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-400 mb-1">
            <span>Pillar 01</span>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Purchasing Power Dynamics</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
            1. The Rupee Illusion: Why Nominal Crore Goals Lead to Severe Shortfalls
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
            Standard calculators show you wealth in inflated future rupees. Here is how inflation quietly cuts your purchasing power in half every 12 years.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              When a commercial SIP calculator promises that saving ₹25,000 a month will make you a <strong>"Crorepati in 20 years"</strong>, it hides the most crucial detail: what will ₹1 Crore actually buy in 2045? Because prices rise constantly, counting future rupees without adjusting for inflation gives a dangerously false sense of security.
            </p>
            
            <!-- Opening the Black Box: Inflation & Real Return -->
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 shadow-sm space-y-4">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-800 pb-2">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-400">
                  Opening the Black Box: How Real Return is Calculated
                </span>
                <span class="text-xs text-navy-500 font-mono">The Fisher Equation</span>
              </div>

              <!-- 3-Step Visual Machinery -->
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
                <!-- Step 1: Input -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-navy-50/70 dark:bg-navy-900/60 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-navy-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-navy-200 dark:bg-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs">1</span>
                    <span>What Goes In</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
                    <strong>12% Market Return</strong> on your mutual funds, along with a baseline <strong>6% Annual Inflation</strong> in consumer prices.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 2: Inside the Engine -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-gold-50/60 dark:bg-gold-950/30 border border-gold-200 dark:border-gold-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-300 font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-gold-200 dark:bg-gold-800 text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-200 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">2</span>
                    <span>Inside the Engine</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
                    You don't simply subtract (12% - 6% = 6%). Instead, ₹1.12 of market gain is divided by ₹1.06 of higher store prices:
                    <span class="block mt-1 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white bg-white dark:bg-navy-900 p-1 rounded border border-gold-200 dark:border-gold-800">
                      (1.12 / 1.06) - 1 = +5.66%
                    </span>
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 3: What Comes Out -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50/60 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-emerald-200 dark:bg-emerald-800 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">3</span>
                    <span>Real Rupee Impact</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300">
                    Your real wealth grows at <strong>5.66% a year</strong> above store prices. Any plan assuming flat 12% purchasing power will fall short by more than half.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white pt-2">
              The 12-Year Halving Rule: Why Cash Melts Over Time
            </h4>
            <p>
              Under a standard 6% annual inflation rate, the purchasing power of your money cuts in half roughly every <strong>11.9 years</strong> (derived from the natural doubling rule: <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-navy-100 dark:bg-navy-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">ln(2) / ln(1.06)</span>).
            </p>
            <p>
              This means a ₹1.00 Crore balance 20 years from now will buy only what <strong>₹31.18 Lakh</strong> buys today. If your retirement lifestyle requires ₹1 Crore in today's living standards, your nominal bank account target must actually be <strong>₹3.21 Crore</strong>.
            </p>

            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white pt-2">
              "Aspirational Inflation": Where 6% Inflation Underestimates Reality
            </h4>
            <p>
              The government's official 6% inflation figure tracks a basic basket of staple goods like rice, milk, and petrol. But the major goals you are investing for experience much steeper price jumps:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
              <li><strong>Higher Education & Professional Colleges:</strong> College tuition in India has historically grown at 10% to 12% annually (doubling every 6 to 7 years).</li>
              <li><strong>Quality Private Healthcare:</strong> Medical inflation averages 12% to 14% a year due to modern diagnostic equipment and specialized treatments.</li>
              <li><strong>Tier-1 City Housing:</strong> Desirable residential property near major economic hubs experiences 8% to 11% long-term cost escalation.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-navy-50/80 dark:bg-navy-900/60 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-4">
              <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white">
                What ₹1 Crore Buys Over Time (at 6% Inflation)
              </h4>
              <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs">
                <div class="flex justify-between pb-1.5 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Year 0 (Today):</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white">₹1.00 Crore full value</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between pb-1.5 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In 5 Years:</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-200">₹74.73 Lakh purchasing power</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between pb-1.5 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In 10 Years:</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-200">₹55.84 Lakh</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between pb-1.5 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In 15 Years:</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-200">₹41.73 Lakh</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between pb-1.5 border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In 20 Years:</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-400">₹31.18 Lakh</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between">
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In 25 Years:</span>
                  <span class="font-bold text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400">₹23.30 Lakh</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-gold-300 dark:border-gold-800/60 bg-gold-50/40 dark:bg-gold-950/20 text-xs text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-300 space-y-1.5">
              <span class="font-bold text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-300 block">The Engine's Core Standard</span>
              <p>
                Every number in this engine is calculated in <strong>Today's Real Money (Purchasing Power)</strong>. You will never be misled by nominal numbers that shrink when you actually go to spend them.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 2: The Exponential Power of Career Step-Up -->
      <article class="scroll-mt-8 space-y-6 pt-8 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
        <div class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mb-1">
            <span>Pillar 02</span>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Human Capital & Career Growth</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
            2. The Career Step-Up: Turning Your Promotions into Lasting Wealth
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
            Why keeping your monthly SIP flat causes your real savings to shrink, and how a small annual increase creates an explosion in final wealth.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200 leading-relaxed">
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
              The Two Types of Wealth: Earning Ability vs Investment Corpus
            </h4>
            <p>
              Throughout your career, your net worth consists of two distinct components:
            </p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
              <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 space-y-1">
                <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white block">1. Earning Ability (Human Capital)</span>
                <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 block">The total salary and income you will earn over your working life. High when you are young; gradually goes to zero when you retire.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 space-y-1">
                <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white block">2. Investment Corpus (Financial Capital)</span>
                <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 block">The assets you own (mutual funds, bonds, gold). Starts small, but must grow large enough to pay for your life when your salary stops.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>
              A fixed, flat SIP fails because as your salary doubles with promotions and experience, an unadjusted ₹25,000 monthly investment becomes an increasingly tiny fraction of your income. Meanwhile, inflation means that ₹25,000 buys fewer and fewer fund units every passing year.
            </p>

            <!-- Opening the Black Box: Step-Up Math -->
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 shadow-sm space-y-4">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-800 pb-2">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400">
                  Opening the Black Box: The Step-Up Multiplier Engine
                </span>
                <span class="text-xs text-navy-500 font-mono">Geometric Accumulation</span>
              </div>

              <!-- 3-Step Visual Machinery -->
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
                <!-- Step 1: Input -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-navy-50/70 dark:bg-navy-900/60 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-navy-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-navy-200 dark:bg-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs">1</span>
                    <span>What Goes In</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
                    Starting with ₹25,000/month, you commit to increasing your SIP by just <strong>5% above inflation</strong> each year whenever you get an annual salary raise.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 2: Inside the Engine -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50/60 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-emerald-200 dark:bg-emerald-800 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">2</span>
                    <span>Inside the Engine</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
                    Instead of a flat stream, your savings grow alongside your salary curve. Year 1 deploys ₹3 Lakh, Year 5 deploys ₹3.65 Lakh, and Year 10 deploys ₹4.88 Lakh (in today's money).
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 3: What Comes Out -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-gold-50/60 dark:bg-gold-950/30 border border-gold-200 dark:border-gold-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-300 font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-gold-200 dark:bg-gold-800 text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-200 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">3</span>
                    <span>Real Rupee Impact</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-gold-800 dark:text-gold-300">
                    Over 20 years, your final wealth jumps from <strong>₹1.42 Crore to ₹2.45 Crore</strong>—an extra <strong>+₹1.03 Crore (+72.5%)</strong> in real wealth created without increasing your starting burden.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white pt-2">
              The "50% Promotion Protocol"
            </h4>
            <p>
              The easiest way to sustain a step-up without feeling pinched is the <strong>50% Rule</strong>: whenever you receive an annual increment or bonus, commit exactly half of the increase to boosting your automated SIP, and keep the remaining 50% for upgrading your lifestyle. You enjoy your hard work today while automatically building freedom for tomorrow.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-navy-50/80 dark:bg-navy-900/60 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-3">
              <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white">
                Final Wealth Comparison (20 Years)
              </h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
                Starting at ₹25,000/mo in real purchasing power:
              </p>
              <div class="space-y-2 text-xs">
                <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
                  <div class="flex justify-between">
                    <span class="font-bold text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">0% Real Step-Up (Flat)</span>
                    <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white">₹1.42 Cr</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="text-navy-500 text-xs">Baseline accumulation</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-800">
                  <div class="flex justify-between">
                    <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300">+3% Real Step-Up / Yr</span>
                    <span class="font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">₹1.98 Cr</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 text-xs">+39.4% extra wealth</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-gold-50 dark:bg-gold-950/40 border border-gold-300 dark:border-gold-800">
                  <div class="flex justify-between">
                    <span class="font-bold text-gold-800 dark:text-gold-300">+5% Real Step-Up / Yr</span>
                    <span class="font-bold text-gold-900 dark:text-gold-200">₹2.45 Cr</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-400 text-xs">+72.5% extra wealth</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-navy-100/70 dark:bg-navy-800/80 border border-navy-300 dark:border-navy-700">
                  <div class="flex justify-between">
                    <span class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">+8% Real Step-Up / Yr</span>
                    <span class="font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white">₹3.38 Cr</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-300 text-xs">+138% multiplier on capital</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 3: Market Volatility & Average Price Engine -->
      <article class="scroll-mt-8 space-y-6 pt-8 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
        <div class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400 mb-1">
            <span>Pillar 03</span>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Market Volatility & Timing</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-950 dark:text-white">
            3. The Volatility Secret: Why Early Crashes Help You, But Late Crashes Hurt You
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
            How monthly investing turns market drops into a unit-buying superpower, and why you must shift gears as you near your retirement date.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-sm sm:text-base text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200 leading-relaxed">
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950 dark:text-white pt-2">
              Why Your Average Purchase Price is Always Lower Than the Market Average
            </h4>
            <p>
              When you invest a fixed ₹25,000 every month regardless of news headlines, something remarkable happens: when the market falls, your ₹25,000 buys <em>more fund units</em> at a discount. When the market is expensive, you automatically buy <em>fewer units</em>.
            </p>

            <!-- Opening the Black Box: Rupee Cost Averaging -->
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 shadow-sm space-y-4">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-800 pb-2">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-400">
                  Opening the Black Box: The Rupee-Cost Averaging Engine
                </span>
                <span class="text-xs text-navy-500 font-mono">The Harmonic Mean Law</span>
              </div>

              <!-- 3-Step Visual Machinery -->
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
                <!-- Step 1: Input -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-navy-50/70 dark:bg-navy-900/60 border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-navy-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-navy-200 dark:bg-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs">1</span>
                    <span>What Goes In</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
                    A fixed ₹25,000 invested every month while market prices bounce between high (₹100/unit) and low (₹50/unit during a crash).
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Step 2: Inside the Engine -->
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-sky-50/60 dark:bg-sky-950/30 border border-sky-200 dark:border-sky-800 space-y-1.5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-300 font-bold">
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-sky-200 dark:bg-sky-800 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-200 flex items-center justify-center text-xs">2</span>
                    <span>Inside the Engine</span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
                    At ₹100, you buy 250 units. At ₹50, you buy 500 units. You spent ₹50,000 total to acquire 750 units.
